= Teamwork

== Team formation

Our team consists of six members with complementary backgrounds: Arianna in Artificial Intelligence, Matteo, Sara and Elisa in Data Science, and Alessia in Human-Computer Interaction, all within Computer Science, while Emilio studied Engineering Physics and now specialises in High-Performance Computing.

These skills covered ComplAI's main areas: regulatory data processing, AI architecture, user experience, and scalability. Some members had also previously founded a startup, giving the group direct experience of the constraints early-stage ventures face.

== Working process

Our first idea was not ComplAI: we started from a blockchain-based crypto transaction monitoring concept (see the #link(<sec-ideation>)[Ideation] section for why it did not survive contact with the market). Interviews and a feasibility analysis showed the real pain point was elsewhere: companies could not keep up with regulation in the first place, not that transaction data could not be trusted. That realisation pushed us towards ComplAI, a broader and more urgent concern than the niche security tool we started with. The pivot set the tone for how we worked afterward: market evidence mattered more than loyalty to our first idea.

Once we had ComplAI as our direction, things did not fall into place feature by feature. We went back and forth on what the product should promise, what we could charge, and who would pay, changing our minds on all three more than once. By the time we reached the landing page and pitch deck, that back-and-forth had already happened behind the scenes: the finished value proposition is the result of several earlier versions we scrapped.

Work was split based on who was best suited for what, without letting that turn into six people working in isolation. We checked in regularly, flagged what was not working instead of pushing it through, and kept adjusting as we understood the problem better.

== Individual contributions

We defined our role based on our personalities discussed during the activity organized by Prof. Dr. Thomas Funke.

Sara acted as the Boss, making the call when we got stuck arguing in circles. Elisa was our Organiser, chasing deadlines and making sure meetings happened and led somewhere. Emilio was the Maker, building things rather than just discussing them, from the service structure to the landing page. Matteo was our Consultant, mostly by disagreeing with us: he pushed back on assumptions and flagged risks we would have missed. Alessia was the Artist, responsible for how ComplAI looks and the one most likely to suggest something weirder. Arianna was the Helper and Enthusiast, providing support where needed and keeping the group's mood up under stress.
